      "markdownBody": "# CodeRabbit findings for PAN-5499 (PR #5580)\n\nCodeRabbit posted 6 inline finding(s). CodeRabbit is advisory: nothing waits for these,\nbut each one gets an answer, either a fix or a reply with your reason.\n\n- Thread 4623953087 · .pan/drafts/PAN-5499.md:284 [Minor]: Describe the global setting as an inherited default.\n  https://github.com/eltmon/overdeck/pull/5580#discussion_r4623953087\n- Thread 4623953089 · .pan/drafts/PAN-5499.md:313 [Minor]: Resolve the prohibited changelog edits before prescribing WI-5.\n  https://github.com/eltmon/overdeck/pull/5580#discussion_r4623953089\n- Thread 4623953093 · changelog.mdx:2 [Minor]: Keep direct edits out of the changelog header.\n  https://github.com/eltmon/overdeck/pull/5580#discussion_r4623953093\n- Thread 4623953097 · changelog.mdx:8 [Minor]: Include the installed package version in the sync startup gate.\n  https://github.com/eltmon/overdeck/pull/5580#discussion_r4623953097\n- Thread 4623953100 · vision.mdx:104 [Minor]: Align the bot identity with the operating prompts.\n  https://github.com/eltmon/overdeck/pull/5580#discussion_r4623953100\n- Thread 4623953104 · vision.mdx:132 [Major]: Describe the global setting as a fallback, not an unconditional hold.\n  https://github.com/eltmon/overdeck/pull/5580#discussion_r4623953104\n\n## What to do\n\n1. Read each thread (open its link, or the code at the path and line).\n2. If you agree with a finding, fix it.\n3. If you reject a finding, reply on its thread with your reason:\n   `gh api repos/eltmon/overdeck/pulls/5580/comments/<thread id>/replies -f body=\"<reason>\"`\n4. If you changed code: run the quality gates on what you touched, commit, push, then run `pan review request PAN-5499 -m \"CodeRabbit <thread ids>: <what you changed>\"`.\n   If you only replied, you are done.\n5. If PR #5580 has already merged when you read this, stop: after the merge Overdeck files a follow-up issue\n   for every thread with no reply, no later commit to its file, and no re-review request naming its thread id."
